# Environment Configuration Template

Copy this to `.env` in your backend directory and fill in your values.

```env
# =================================================================
# MONGODB DATABASE CONFIGURATION
# =================================================================
# Get your MongoDB connection string from:
# https://cloud.mongodb.com/v2/[project-id]/clusters
# 
# Format: mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster-name.mongodb.net/database-name
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://your_username:your_password@cluster-name.mongodb.net/budgetdb?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# =================================================================
# JWT AUTHENTICATION
# =================================================================
# Use a strong, random string (min 32 characters)
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key_min_32_chars_1234567890

# =================================================================
# SERVER CONFIGURATION
# =================================================================
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development

# =================================================================
# N8N AUTOMATION CONFIGURATION
# =================================================================
# Local n8n instance
# N8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5678/webhook

# n8n Cloud (recommended for production)
# Get your base URL from n8n Cloud dashboard
N8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL=https://your-org.n8n.cloud/webhook

# n8n authentication (if needed)
# N8N_API_KEY=your_n8n_api_key
# N8N_AUTH_TOKEN=your_n8n_auth_token

# =================================================================
# EJOCHAT API (Kinyarwanda-first AI by Ejo Labs)
# =================================================================
# Get your API key from: https://ejolabs.com/tenant
# Plans: Ejo Free (50 req/day), Basic (2500 RWF/bundle), Business, Enterprise
EJOCHAT_API_KEY=your_ejochat_api_key
EJOCHAT_BASE_URL=https://api.ejolabs.com/api/v1

# =================================================================
# AI/ML SERVICES (Optional - for n8n workflows)
# =================================================================
# OpenAI API Key (for price predictions, recommendations, etc.)
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-your_openai_api_key

# Anthropic API Key (alternative to OpenAI)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your_anthropic_key

# =================================================================
# VENDOR/MARKET INTEGRATIONS (Optional - for price fetching)
# =================================================================
# Walmart API
WALMART_API_KEY=your_walmart_api_key
WALMART_API_URL=https://api.walmartapis.com

# Amazon Product Advertising API
AMAZON_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_amazon_key
AMAZON_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_amazon_secret

# Google Shopping Integration
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_google_api_key

# =================================================================
# EXTERNAL SERVICES
# =================================================================
# Email Service (for alerts/notifications - optional)
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your_email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your_app_password
SMTP_FROM=noreply@budget-system.com

# SendGrid (alternative email service)
# SENDGRID_API_KEY=your_sendgrid_api_key

# Twilio (for SMS notifications - optional)
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=your_account_sid
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your_auth_token
# TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=+1234567890

# =================================================================
# LOGGING & MONITORING
# =================================================================
LOG_LEVEL=info
SENTRY_DSN=https://your_sentry_dsn@sentry.io/project_id

# =================================================================
# SECURITY
# =================================================================
# CORS configuration
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173,https://yourdomain.com

# Rate limiting
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW=15
RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=100

# Session timeout (in milliseconds)
SESSION_TIMEOUT=3600000

# =================================================================
# FEATURE FLAGS
# =================================================================
# Enable/disable features
FEATURE_AI_PREDICTIONS=true
FEATURE_MARKET_TRACKING=true
FEATURE_ANOMALY_DETECTION=true
FEATURE_EMAIL_ALERTS=false
FEATURE_SMS_ALERTS=false

# =================================================================
# DEVELOPMENT & DEBUGGING
# =================================================================
# Set to true for verbose logging
DEBUG=false
DEBUG_VERBOSE=false

# Mock n8n responses (for testing without n8n)
MOCK_N8N=false
MOCK_N8N_PREDICT_PRICE=2.30
MOCK_N8N_POTENTIAL_SAVINGS=50

# =================================================================
# DATABASE BACKUPS & MAINTENANCE
# =================================================================
# Automatic backup (daily, weekly, monthly)
BACKUP_FREQUENCY=daily
BACKUP_STORAGE=s3

# AWS S3 for backups
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_aws_key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_aws_secret
AWS_S3_BUCKET=budget-system-backups
AWS_S3_REGION=us-east-1

# =================================================================
# EXTERNAL WEBHOOKS (Callbacks from n8n)
# =================================================================
# Allow n8n to send data back to your API
N8N_CALLBACK_URL=http://your-backend.com/api/webhooks/n8n
N8N_CALLBACK_SECRET=your_n8n_callback_secret

# =================================================================
# ANALYTICS & BUSINESS INTELLIGENCE
# =================================================================
# Google Analytics 4
GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# Mixpanel
MIXPANEL_TOKEN=your_mixpanel_token

# =================================================================
# PAYMENT & MONETIZATION (Optional)
# =================================================================
# Stripe
STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_your_stripe_key
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your_stripe_key
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_your_webhook_secret

# =================================================================
# THIRD-PARTY INTEGRATIONS
# =================================================================
# Firebase (optional - for real-time updates)
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_firebase_project
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=your_firebase_private_key
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase@your_project.iam.gserviceaccount.com

# Redis (for caching)
REDIS_HOST=localhost
REDIS_PORT=6379
REDIS_PASSWORD=your_redis_password

# =================================================================
# COMPLIANCE & SECURITY
# =================================================================
# Data retention (days)
DATA_RETENTION_DAYS=365

# Encryption
ENCRYPTION_KEY=your_encryption_key_32_chars_required

# PII Handling
MASK_PII=true
ENCRYPT_SENSITIVE_DATA=true

# =================================================================
# PRODUCTION ONLY
# =================================================================
# When NODE_ENV=production, additional checks apply

# Certificate paths for HTTPS
TLS_CERT_PATH=/etc/ssl/certs/cert.pem
TLS_KEY_PATH=/etc/ssl/private/key.pem

# Domain
DOMAIN=yourdomain.com

# =================================================================
# NOTES
# =================================================================
# 1. Never commit .env to Git - add to .gitignore
# 2. Use different API keys for dev/staging/production
# 3. Rotate API keys regularly
# 4. Use strong, unique passwords
# 5. Store secrets securely (AWS Secrets Manager, Azure Key Vault, etc.)
# 6. Use .env.example for version control (without sensitive values)
```

---

## Setup Instructions

### Step 1: Create `.env` File
```bash
cd backend
touch .env
```

### Step 2: Copy Template
Copy the template above into `.env`

### Step 3: Fill in Required Values

#### MongoDB URI
1. Go to https://cloud.mongodb.com
2. Create a cluster
3. Get connection string
4. Paste into `MONGODB_URI`

#### JWT Secret
```bash
# Generate a secure JWT secret
openssl rand -base64 32
```

#### N8N Webhook URL
- **Local:** `http://localhost:5678/webhook`
- **Cloud:** Get from n8n dashboard

#### OpenAI API Key
1. Go to https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
2. Create API key
3. Paste into `OPENAI_API_KEY`

### Step 4: Verify Configuration
```bash
# Test connection
npm run test:env
```

---

## Environment by Deployment Stage

### Development (.env.development)
```env
NODE_ENV=development
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/budget-dev
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173
DEBUG=true
MOCK_N8N=false
```

### Staging (.env.staging)
```env
NODE_ENV=staging
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://...staging...
CORS_ORIGIN=https://staging.yourdomain.com
DEBUG=false
MOCK_N8N=false
```

### Production (.env.production)
```env
NODE_ENV=production
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://...production...
CORS_ORIGIN=https://yourdomain.com
DEBUG=false
MOCK_N8N=false
SENTRY_DSN=https://...
```

---

## Security Checklist

✅ `MONGODB_URI` - Secure connection with credentials  
✅ `JWT_SECRET` - Strong, random, 32+ characters  
✅ `OPENAI_API_KEY` - Never committed to Git  
✅ `CORS_ORIGIN` - Limited to trusted domains  
✅ `N8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL` - HTTPS in production  
✅ API Keys rotated regularly  
✅ `.env` in `.gitignore`  
✅ Separate keys for each environment  

---

## `.gitignore` Entry
```
# .gitignore

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.key
*.pem
node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
```

