## Loading Environment Variables in Code

```javascript
// In your Node.js app
import dotenv from 'dotenv';
dotenv.config();

// Access variables
const mongoUri = process.env.MONGODB_URI;
const jwtSecret = process.env.JWT_SECRET;
const n8nWebhook = process.env.N8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL;
```

---

## Troubleshooting

| Issue | Solution |
|-------|----------|
| `undefined` values | Check `.env` file exists and is loaded |
| MongoDB connection fails | Verify `MONGODB_URI` and network access |
| n8n webhooks timeout | Check `N8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL` is correct |
| API keys not working | Verify keys in dashboard, regenerate if needed |
| CORS errors | Ensure `CORS_ORIGIN` matches frontend URL |

---

## Environment Variable Validation Script

Add to `package.json`:
```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "test:env": "node scripts/validate-env.js"
  }
}
```

Create `scripts/validate-env.js`:
```javascript
const required = [
  'MONGODB_URI',
  'JWT_SECRET',
  'N8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL',
];

const missing = required.filter(key => !process.env[key]);

if (missing.length > 0) {
  console.error('❌ Missing required environment variables:');
  missing.forEach(key => console.error(`   - ${key}`));
  process.exit(1);
}

console.log('✅ All required environment variables configured');
```

---

## Production Deployment Checklist

Before deploying to production:

- [ ] Use strong, unique `JWT_SECRET`
- [ ] Enable HTTPS (certificates configured)
- [ ] Set `NODE_ENV=production`
- [ ] Limit `CORS_ORIGIN` to your domain
- [ ] Use production MongoDB instance
- [ ] Configure n8n Cloud (not local)
- [ ] Set up monitoring & logging (Sentry, etc.)
- [ ] Configure backups
- [ ] Test all API keys
- [ ] Enable rate limiting
- [ ] Set up SSL/TLS
- [ ] Use environment-specific configs
- [ ] Secrets in secure vault (AWS, Azure, etc.)

---

**Never share or commit `.env` files!**

For more details, see: `BUDGET_SYSTEM_SETUP.md` and `N8N_SETUP_GUIDE.md`
